<title>UK: Lehman sets warrants on five German stocks.</title>
<headline>Lehman sets warrants on five German stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers Finance has issued five million European-style mark-denominated call warrants each on shares of Bankgesellschaft Berlin AG, Bayer AG, Hoechst AG, Deutsche Telekom AG and Metro AG, lead manager Lehman Brothers Bankaus AG said.</p>
<p> MATURITY DATE   30.DEC.97		 PAYDATE	10.MAR.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   FFT/STUT/DUES	   MIN EXER LOT 100 * * * *</p>
<p> WARRANT     STRIKE    SPOT REF    ISSUE    X-TRA LEVEL</p>
<p> BG BERLIN   32.5	32.33	 4.10     30.5</p>
<p> BAYER	 75	  69.6	  4.74     65</p>
<p> HOECHST     75	  71.8	  6.51     75</p>
<p> TELEKOM     34	  32.4	  4.22     30.5</p>
<p> METRO	150	 140	    8.95    125</p>
<p> NOTES	WARRANT HOLDERS WILL RECEIVE AN EXTRA 10 DEM</p>
<p>		IN THE EVENT THAT THE STOCK PRICE DOES NOT FALL</p>
<p>		AT OR BELOW THE &quot;X-TRA LEVEL&quot; BETWEEN 06.MAR.97</p>
<p>		AND 30.DEC.97</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
